    "stem": "Show that\n\n(i) \\(\\sin^{-1}\\left(2x\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\right) = 2\\sin^{-1} x,\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\le x \\le \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\)\n\n(ii) \\(\\sin^{-1}\\left(2x\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\right) = 2\\cos^{-1} x,\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\le x \\le 1\\)",
    "solution": "(i) Let \\(x = \\sin\\theta\\). Then \\(\\sin^{-1} x = \\theta\\). We have\n\n\\(\\sin^{-1}\\left(2x\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\right) = \\sin^{-1}\\left(2\\sin\\theta\\sqrt{1-\\sin^2\\theta}\\right)\\)\n\n\\(= \\sin^{-1}(2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta) = \\sin^{-1}(\\sin 2\\theta) = 2\\theta\\)\n\n\\(= 2\\sin^{-1} x\\)\n\n(ii) Take \\(x = \\cos\\theta\\), then proceeding as above, we get \\(\\sin^{-1}\\left(2x\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\right) = 2\\cos^{-1} x\\)."
